{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b5846eae7879a0289e577bf5c3019cf394792c01282846305c2cfad757fea555","digest":{"component_or_area":"op-cert service config","key_entities":["REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH","src/rebar/opcert_service/config.py","src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py","_private_key_env()","OpcertServiceConfig.from_env()","compose_signer","keyprov.py","workspace.py","tests/unit/test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py","scripts/gen_env_registry.py","docs/env-vars.md"],"problem_keywords":["credential hardening","environment variable leakage","secret management","inline PEM","process environment"],"propositions":["REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY environment variable remains in os.environ after OpcertServiceConfig.from_env() reads it, exposing the inline PEM to child processes and environment dumps","The inline PEM secret is passed to subprocess.run calls (ssh-keygen, git) that inherit the environment because neither _validate_key_file nor _git pass an explicit env parameter","Consuming the environment variable at the read boundary in _private_key_env() by popping it after capture removes the secret from process environment and child process inheritance after config load","A test contract pins consume-once semantics so that a second from_env() call in the same process returns None and does not raise, preventing silent key loss if a reload path is added later"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787404648053974001,"uuid":"32f926e4-b887-484f-99ae-9dc443560e37"}